# Procedural Textures Skill

> Gera texturas PBR proceduralmente via GLSL shaders (TexGen-style) para Three.js.
> Substitui texturas canvas por shaders GPU-accelerados.

## Quando usar
- Quando texturas procedural canvas são insuficientes (nota <97)
- Para texturas PBR (albedo, normal, roughness, metallic)
- Para texturas animadas (lava, água, fogo)

## Como usar

### 1. Criar textura procedural
```js
// shaders/procedural.glsl - exemplo de textura de concreto
uniform float uTime;
uniform vec2 uResolution;

float noise(vec2 p) {
  return fract(sin(dot(p, vec2(12.9898, 78.233))) * 43758.5453);
}

void main() {
  vec2 uv = gl_FragCoord.xy / uResolution;

  // Base concrete color
  vec3 color = vec3(0.35, 0.35, 0.38);

  // Add noise variation
  float n = noise(uv * 10.0) * 0.1;
  color += n;

  // Add cracks
  float crack = smoothstep(0.48, 0.5, noise(uv * 50.0));
  color -= crack * 0.2;

  // Add stains
  float stain = smoothstep(0.7, 0.8, noise(uv * 8.0));
  color -= stain * 0.15;

  gl_FragColor = vec4(color, 1.0);
}
```

### 2. Aplicar no Three.js
```js
import * as THREE from 'three';

const material = new THREE.ShaderMaterial({
  uniforms: {
    uTime: { value: 0 },
    uResolution: { value: new THREE.Vector2(512, 512) }
  },
  vertexShader: `
    varying vec2 vUv;
    void main() {
      vUv = uv;
      gl_Position = projectionMatrix * modelViewMatrix * vec4(position, 1.0);
    }
  `,
  fragmentShader: concreteShader
});
```

## Referências
- TexGen: https://github.com/tonym128/texgen
- PTG: https://github.com/andraswebcode/ptg
- Noise textures: https://lumitree.art/blog/noise-texture

## Exemplos de shaders
Ver `shaders/` directory para exemplos prontos:
- `concrete.glsl` - concreto com rachaduras
- `metal.glsl` - metal com arranhões
- `brick.glsl` - tijolos procedural
- `lava.glsl` - lava animada
